{"id": "murray:sex:need_low", "reasoning": "Murray's low pole for sex marks someone with a weak drive toward sexual pleasure or contact. Today such a person is simply sexually uninterested, with little appetite for sexual activity.", "labels": ["Sexually indifferent", "Low-libido"], "gloss": "This means having little interest in sex, showing little drive toward sexual pursuit or physical intimacy.", "polysemy": false},
{"id": "murray:succorance:need_high", "reasoning": "Succorance is the need to be nursed, supported and protected by a sympathetic other. A person with a strong need for it today is someone who leans heavily on others for comfort and reassurance.", "labels": ["Dependent", "Comfort-seeking"], "gloss": "This means constantly seeking comfort, support and protection from others, wanting to be looked after when troubled.", "polysemy": true},
{"id": "murray:succorance:need_low", "reasoning": "The low pole of succorance describes someone who feels little wish to be helped or comforted and copes with trouble alone. Today we call such a person self-reliant.", "labels": ["Self-reliant", "Stoical"], "gloss": "This means handling difficulties on one's own, neither wanting nor seeking help, comfort or reassurance from others.", "polysemy": false},
{"id": "murray:understanding:need_high", "reasoning": "Murray's high need for understanding is a drive to ask general questions and pursue theory, analysis and generalization. Today this person is analytical and intellectually inquisitive.", "labels": ["Analytical", "Theoretical", "Inquisitive"], "gloss": "This means constantly asking general questions and enjoying theory, analysis, and drawing broad conclusions from particular facts.", "polysemy": false},
{"id": "murray:understanding:need_low", "reasoning": "The low pole of understanding describes someone with little interest in theory or in grasping why things are as they are. Today we would call such a person incurious about ideas and explanations.", "labels": ["Incurious", "Unanalytical"], "gloss": "This means showing little interest in explanations or theory, taking things at face value without asking why they happen.", "polysemy": false}
]}
